WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:04.920
There's no denying the first Star Wars spinoff
film is a major hit.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:08.700
But looking back at the early trailers for
Rogue One, it's obvious the story changed

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.490
a lot during its reportedly extensive reshoots.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:12.490
So what's different?

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:16.260
Here's a look at some misleading trailer moments
that didn't add up in Rogue One.

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:17.610
Jyn's perp walk

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:22.120
In the first trailer, Jyn is led into the
Rebel base in handcuffs, and then has a tense

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.930
back and forth with Mon Mothma:

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:27.050
"On your own from the age of 15.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:29.100
Reckless, aggressive, and undisciplined."

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.600
"This is a rebellion isn't it?

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:36.140
I rebel."

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.220
Afterwards, Mon Mothma gives Jyn her marching
orders:

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:42.170
"We have a mission for you.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:48.920
A major weapons test is imminent, and we need
to know what it is and how to destroy it."

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:50.470
Along with this brief pep talk:

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:54.650
"Our Rebellion is all that remains to push
back the Empire."

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:58.840
Just one thing, though… none of this is
actually in the final film, with the exposition

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:03.280
about Jyn's history coming during her confrontation
with Saw Gerrera instead.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.570
Speaking of which...

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:05.680
What happened to Saw?

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:08.609
Remember that foreboding voiceover from Saw
in the trailer?

00:01:08.609 --> 00:01:11.090
"What will you do when they catch you?

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.579
What will you do if they break you?

00:01:13.579 --> 00:01:19.530
If you continue to fight, what will you become?"

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:20.530
Exciting.

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:21.530
Exhilarating.

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:25.380
Completely missing from the movie, along with
a bit where Jyn seems to be trying to convince

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:29.100
Forest Whitaker's character to fight the good
fight — instead of the other way around:

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.820
"This is our chance to make a real difference."

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:37.780
Oh, and there's the fact that Saw used to
be bald and not quite so mangled in the previews.

00:01:37.789 --> 00:01:41.259
We're not sure what the filmmakers originally
intended for Saw, but it seems to have been

00:01:41.259 --> 00:01:43.289
quite different from what they ended up with.

00:01:43.289 --> 00:01:44.409
Welcome to Jedha

00:01:44.409 --> 00:01:48.200
One of the coolest shots from the first trailers
was this clip of a broken down Jedi statue

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.409
on the moon of Jedha.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:52.810
But while we do see the statue in the film,
it's not this shot.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:56.450
It's not the only thing about Jedha missing
from the finished film: this brief clip of

00:01:56.450 --> 00:02:01.139
captured X-Wing pilots being marched to their
doom by stormtroopers is gone too.

00:02:01.139 --> 00:02:02.929
The entire ending is different

00:02:02.929 --> 00:02:06.600
One thing we can glean from the trailers is
that they rewrote the entire ending of the

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.600
movie.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:10.259
This awesome bit where Jyn faces off against
a TIE fighter?

00:02:10.259 --> 00:02:14.599
That's gone, as is this iconic shot of Jyn
standing in a hallway looking badass.

00:02:14.599 --> 00:02:18.360
And left on the cutting room floor is this
bit where Krennic gets his cape dirty down

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.170
on the bloody beaches of Scarif.

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:22.739
But the biggest clue as to why all those shots
are missing?

00:02:22.739 --> 00:02:26.599
Well, this clip of Jyn running along the beach
carrying the plans to the Death Star points

00:02:26.599 --> 00:02:31.060
to a major rewrite, since in the final film
she transmits them from the tower and doesn't

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:32.519
fight on the beach at all.

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:36.290
We're not sure why they changed the ending,
but it's clear the reshoots altered almost

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:37.290
everything.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.290
More Darth Vader

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:43.260
Finally, the early trailers offered up our
first peeks at Darth Vader's cinematic return,

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:47.319
but it's obvious there were at least one or
two additional Vader scenes that were filmed,

00:02:47.319 --> 00:02:48.900
including a different exchange with Krennic.

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:52.349
It begs the question: Why not include as much
Vader as possible?

00:02:52.349 --> 00:02:54.569
Everyone knows that Darth Vader makes everything
better.

00:02:54.569 --> 00:02:59.450
"Check this out...here's...I've seen better
first pitches but, ya know."

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:00.989
"Nice block by Mr. Red though."

00:03:00.989 --> 00:03:02.959
"Ya he did block it, good technique."

00:03:02.959 --> 00:03:03.959
That, and pizza.

00:03:03.959 --> 00:03:05.159
Now I want pizza.

00:03:05.159 --> 00:03:06.159
Thanks for watching!

00:03:06.159 --> 00:03:08.409
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:03:08.409 --> 00:03:10.749
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

